    txt('PORT_CONTRACT_R3.md',"# Gemensamt kollagenreferenskontrakt R3\n\nPENDING_INDEPENDENT_REVIEW. `shared_reference_r3` is a synthetic forward model.\n\n| Port/state | Unit and reference | Operation/source | Status |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| C and trace(Q_U+Q_I+Q_M) | intact collagen mass per fixed registered reference volume, dimensionless | Same initial0, B and lambda in every cell; RESPONSE FV and R3 tensor operator | SYNTHETIC |\n| B | reference mass/day | k_deposit F h(1−C); R3≈5/day is inherited early strength calibration | SYNTHETIC |\n| lambda | 1/day | .008 macrophage; equal proportional removal of U/I/M and D/H/A | SYNTHETIC |\n| U→I→M | reference mass/day | k1 h U and k2 h I; .1/.05 per day, internal fluxes cancel | SYNTHETIC |\n| D/H/A | mol/mol same reference collagen | New collagen gets s=.102 precursor-site equivalents; D→2H with eta or A; k from R4 cell analog | SYNTHETIC transfer |\n| D+2H+A | mol site equivalents/mol reference collagen | s C: chemical site equivalents are different units from collagen mass | DERIVED under declared closures |\n| Strength proxy | %intact | 150 bridge eᵀQ_Me; isotropic75% reference | SYNTHETIC |\n| Chemical strength diagnostic | %intact | 75 C clip((H/C−.003)/.040); scales from R3, no external HP curve | SYNTHETIC, no native law |\n| Native traction/rupture and joint posterior | Pa / unknown | Requires matched connected chemistry×age×angle/anchors | UNKNOWN/null |\n\n`birth_scale` and `turnover_U_I` are explicitly unused historical ports in R3. No extra .03/day loss is added. C is not projected separately from marks; an inadmissible state is rejected with a requirement for smaller dt. R3 updates the same O2/FV state as before; the U/I/M partition does not govern oxygen beyond its shared sum. The isolated fixedC10 reservoir is preserved only as an older diagnostic and is not a second collagen amount in the feedback chain.\n\nThe R3 checkpoint stores reference version, full FVstate, Q, chemical marks, born/removed/initial, hazard/earlystate, grid, clock and laws/config. The R1 checkpoint belongs to a different reference and is rejected by the new solver operator. No history conversion is assumed; the entire prefix has been rebuilt and the cost reported.\n")
    txt('MEASUREMENT_SPEC_R3.md',"# Prioritised measurements after the shared inventory\n\nPENDING_INDEPENDENT_REVIEW. The next shared acquisition must distinguish **collagen quantity, maturation kinetics and load-bearing connectivity**. Mass balance is now locked in the model; it identifies no biological rates. Native information value and actual laboratory cost are UNKNOWN. The following is a prioritisation for acquisition, no order or clinical instruction.\n\n| Priority for the entire chain | Measurement package and consumer | Value unlocked | Inherited cost assumption |\n|---:|---|---|---:|\n| 1 | M2: spatially/time-registered O2, storage, boundary flux, separate viability | Early forcing and O2→cell history; early control variable for later maturation | 3 |\n| 2 | M1: the same incision's gap, separate damage/perfusion widths and radius/pressure/flow map | Three early port transitions; radius distribution needed for r⁴ flow | 8 |\n| 3 | M4 **together with** M5: absolute collagen quantity against a fixed reference, precursor/HP/other crosslinks, age×direction×connected crossings, traction/fracture | Separates reference mass from chemistry and load-bearing marks; directly decisive for the remaining21.811pp | 12+16 |\n| 4 | M3: radius-matched plug, remaining flow/seal/erosion on a longer actual clock | Identifies full haemostasis;120min censoring cannot do that | 5 |\n| 5 | M6: full force/work/new area, contact/release and unique terminal interface ledger | New tool→work/damage; helps only when the missing damage transfer is measured | 20 |\n\nFor **late strength** specifically, the matched M4/M5 package goes first: an O2 acquisition alone does not distinguish precursor budget from mechanical connectivity. Measure collagen mol and dry mass per fixed reference area/volume at7/14/21/28/42/90; keep sample shrinkage and water content separate. Measure newborn precursor inventory and HP/other crosslinks per the same collagen reference and measured turnover/selective loss. In parallel, register age, 3D direction, connected cut-plane crossings, survival of both anchors and full traction–opening/ultimate load. Hold late days and at least one donor out of rate/observation fitting; destructive samples are different samples with shared donor blocking, never a measured continuous course in the same sample. Species/site/clock/assay identities must be preserved.\n\nThe executed chemistry case has s=.102 and eta=.283333. Its H/C≤.01445 even with infinitely fast conversion; R3's proxy plateau needs .043. At least s≈.303529 or a changed yield/birth/removal/observation law is required within these particular closures. **Measure these quantities; do not choose them from strength targets.** The purely mathematical minimum is no estimate of a biological precursor pool. R3 U/I/M and D/H/A are two different marks of the same collagen history; a shared biological maturation generator is still unknown.\n\nR2's frozen information analysis gave M2/M1/M5 scores per relative cost .06325/.02649/.02305; M3 .00430 and M4/M6 zero implemented downstream path. These numbers apply to **the previous R2 model**, not a new R3 posterior. On64 new synthetic scenarios, the risk order changed to M2→M5→M1→M3; M1's kernel lost damage precision. R2's0.5–2× cost interval does not prove that M2 beats M1/M5 under all costs. After the inventory change, M4's absolute quantity measurement gets a concrete C consumer, but a new quantitative R3 design/observation likelihood must be frozen before ranking values are updated. Zero old model score is no measure of scientific disinterest.\n\nPrecisions remain planning requirements: O2 random error2Torr with1Torr shared calibration; gap10µm and damage/perfusion widths25µm with10µm shared registration error from the R2 design. Achieved precision for absolute mol, newborn sites, chemistry×age×connected crossings and native mechanics is missing; it must be determined by pilot variance and reference calibration without invented σ. Put their shared assay/donor/reference errors in the same uncertainty, not in independent margins.\n\nThe energy/area parts from INCISION/BINDINGS/GAP remain: one crack-plane area, unique newly detached area, terminal work separate from bulk/bone/contact, measured tool radii and held-out tool/donor. Γ must not become fracture strength and a strain zone must not become a perfusion/necrosis width. The full work plan is preserved in MEASUREMENT_SPEC_R1.md, MEASUREMENT_SPEC_R2.md and the three source lanes' final specs. No emails or acquisitions have been sent.\n")
    txt('COMMANDS_R3.md',"# Reproduktion av R3\n\nChoose new output destinations. Experiments and tests verify frozen PREREG. Two CPU threads; no network traffic or external HP/abundance consumer in the forward chain.\n\n```bash\nPYTHONDONTWRITEBYTECODE=1 python results/LANE_SURGICAL_SYNTHESIS/experiment_r3.py --out results/LANE_SURGICAL_SYNTHESIS/r3/experiment_REPLAY\nPYTHONDONTWRITEBYTECODE=1 python results/LANE_SURGICAL_SYNTHESIS/tests_r3.py --out results/LANE_SURGICAL_SYNTHESIS/r3/tests_REPLAY\nresults/LANE_SURGICAL_SYNTHESIS/run_chain.sh --inventory shared --mode scenario --config results/LANE_SURGICAL_SYNTHESIS/r3/CONFIG_ALL_R3.json --out results/LANE_SURGICAL_SYNTHESIS/r3/chain_REPLAY\nresults/LANE_SURGICAL_SYNTHESIS/run_chain.sh --resume results/LANE_SURGICAL_SYNTHESIS/r3/experiment_v2/all_R3/checkpoint21.npz --out results/LANE_SURGICAL_SYNTHESIS/r3/restart_REPLAY\n```\n\nThe CLI now uses shared inventory as default; evidence-mode leaves native outcomes null. `surgical_chain.shared.run` is the new Python entry point. `surgical_chain.chain.run(..., inventory='legacy')` (historical API default) preserves the exact R1/R2 construction for rerunning old diagnostics. R1 package files before this round are copied to r3/legacy_package/; all old rawfiles and negative results remain. The experiment's first path error is in EXPERIMENT_v1.log and its code snapshot; experiment_v2 applies. For reproduction from another working directory, the package must be in PYTHONPATH according to run_chain.sh.\n")
